1971 by The Rockefeller University Press</copyright-statement></permissions><abstract><p> The N-B locus affecting tissue culture infectivity with naturally occurring murine leukemia viruses appears to be identical to the <italic>Fv-1</italic> locus described for sensitivity to Friend leukemia virus. Results of tissue culture studies were parallel to results of studies in vivo and indicate that the F-S virus is N-tropic and the F-B virus is NB-tropic. Inbred and partially congenic mouse strains sensitive at <italic>Fv-1</italic> show N-type sensitivity; strains resistant at <italic>Fv-1</italic> show B-type sensitivity. The <italic>Fv-2</italic> locus does not appear to exert significant effect in tissue culture. Knowledge of N-B type has been useful in predicting <italic>Fv-1</italic> sensitivity. </p></abstract></article-meta></front></article>